#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Options when plotting a histogram {#options-when-plotting-a-histogram}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Use the following options for `plot_histogram` to adjust the output graph.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`legend`: Provides a label for the executions. It takes a list of strings "
"used to label each execution's results. This is mostly useful when plotting "
"multiple execution results in the same histogram\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`sort`: Adjusts the order of the bars in the histogram. It can be set to "
"either ascending order with `asc` or descending order with `desc`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`number_to_keep`: Takes an integer for the number of terms to show. The rest"
" are grouped together in a single bar called \"rest\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`color`: Adjusts the color of the bars; takes a string or a list of strings "
"for the colors to use for the bars for each execution\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "`bar_labels`: Adjusts whether labels are printed above the bars\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`figsize`: Takes a tuple of the size in inches to make the output figure\n"
msgstr ""

